<title>POLAND: POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES INCH DOWN AT TENDER.</title>
<headline>POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES INCH DOWN AT TENDER.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills fell 0.01 point at today's primary auction on total demand of 694 million zlotys against an 800 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 598 million zlotys of T-bills.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    ---     95.27    90.89     ---     83.19</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.28)  (90.90)    ---    (83.20)</p>
<p>   new max price    ---     95.40    91.00     ---     83.25</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.41)  (91.02)    ---    (83.32)</p>
<p>   offer		---     300.0    100.0     ---     400.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    ---     339.0    100.3     ---     254.8</p>
<p>   bids accepted    ---     315.8     92.3     ---     189.8</p>
<p>   next auction     ---     400.0    100.0     ---     500.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
